From 0983463a85c9ea80e8c256e7d5ce9888da587f2d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 14:02:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Forge host: friend matches, two people in one Forge game

- Engine: input opponentKind "human" seats a second person instead of a CPU.
  Each seat is its own bridge over the same game (own controller, prompts and
  viewer), served at /state + /action and /seat2/state + /seat2/action, so each
  player only ever receives their own projection. Either seat's concession or
  a natural end finishes both seats and releases any open choice.
- Admission: friend input needs startingPlayer random and no CPU pod seats;
  the receipt records opponentKind and guestViewerId; no CPU policy is applied.
- Gateway: forwards the /seat2 routes behind the same internal token.
- Host: private rooms (POST /api/play/rooms, POST /rooms/join with an invite,
  GET/DELETE /rooms/<id>); 30-minute invites stored only as digests, one open
  room per host, atomic seat claim (room_full), one match per room. The lease
  binds both accounts; MatchAuthority maps each verified account to its seat,
  with per-seat pending commands, receipts and rate limits.
- Tests: tests/friend-match.test.mjs (rooms, seats, races, expiry, results).
  Pins re-bound; verify-inputs and run-static-checks pass.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
